      "strengths_deep_dive": [
        "MCN demonstrates a high level of organizational maturity for its size. The charity achieved a <cite id=\"12\">perfect 100 score for Leadership</cite> from Charity Navigator, reflecting strong strategic clarity. Its financial management is equally robust, with <cite id=\"13\">accountability scores reaching 93.79</cite>. This fiscal discipline allows MCN to maintain a <cite id=\"14\">3-year revenue CAGR of 15.7%</cite>, indicating consistent growth in donor trust and community support. By keeping <cite id=\"15\">fundraising costs low at $0.07 per dollar</cite>, the organization maximizes the impact of its $768,698 revenue base on direct services like <cite id=\"16\">immigrant support and advocacy</cite>."
      ],
      "summary": "The Muslim Community Network (MCN) serves as a vital civic infrastructure for Muslim Americans in New York City. Founded in <cite id=\"1\">2003</cite>, the organization has spent over two decades <cite id=\"2\">shaping the public narrative</cite> through leadership development and civic education. In FY2025, MCN reported <cite id=\"3\">total revenue of $768,698</cite>, reflecting a stable financial base for its advocacy and capacity-building efforts. The organization is distinguished by its <cite id=\"4\">Platinum Seal of Transparency from Candid</cite>, the highest level of disclosure available. MCN operates with a <cite id=\"5\">program expense ratio of 80.6%</cite>, ensuring that every dollar of public support is directed toward its core community initiatives. These programs include the <cite id=\"6\">Impact Academy and Community Safety Track</cite>, which empower youth and families to navigate civic spaces confidently. While MCN is a mid-sized organization, it maintains <cite id=\"7\">8.2 months of working capital</cite>, providing a resilient buffer against economic shifts. For faith-motivated donors, MCN provides a <cite id=\"8\">verified zakat-eligible pathway</cite>, distributing funds across several traditional categories including the poor, the needy, and those in debt.",
